  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Initiatives for Sustainable and Climate Smart Oil Palm Smallholders (NISCOPS) Phase 2 - Solidaridad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NISCOPS programme aims to demonstrate that the palm oil sector can contribute to the SDGs and climate ambitions of the Paris Agreement, whilst also improving the livelihoods of smallholder farmers and workers. The programs vision is as follows: &#x201C;that landscapes where oil palms are grown are managed sustainably and smallholders measurably benefit from their inclusion in palm oil markets&#x201D;.  IDH and Solidaridad execute the program in partnership with the governments of Indonesia, Malaysia, Ghana, Nigeria and the Netherlands. The program applies an integrated approach to selected landscapes in major palm oil producing countries, as well as to major palm oil consumer markets, notably the EU and India. Interventions are directed to smallholder farmers, the private sector and public actors along three different action lines: better incomes; better land use; and inclusive markets.</narrative>
  </description>
